  "assumptions": [
    "PostgreSQL is the target database; uuid primary keys use gen_random_uuid() (pgcrypto/pg13+). Types such as numeric(3,2) and varchar(n) are standard PostgreSQL types.",
    "Every table has exactly one primary key column (id). Junction tables (user_courses, group_members, message_notes) use a surrogate id PK plus a composite unique constraint on their two FK columns, listed in indexes as comma-separated column names.",
    "Composite entries in indexes (e.g. 'group_id,status') denote multi-column indexes; the ones noted as unique (user_courses, note_ratings, group_members, message_notes, courses university_id+code, topics course_id+name) must be created as UNIQUE indexes.",
    "Platform-wide roles (student, moderator, system_admin) are stored in users.platform_role; the Group Admin role is contextual and stored in group_members.role, with the group creator inserted as an active admin member at creation.",
    "Registration is restricted to emails whose domain matches universities.email_domain; accounts stay in pending_verification until a token in email_verification_tokens is consumed.",
    "Passwords are stored only as bcrypt hashes; JWT access tokens are stateless, so no session table is included.",
    "Files are stored in AWS S3; only the object key and metadata are stored in the database. notes.scan_status and notes.status support the virus-scan-before-publish requirement, and the 20 MB limit and PDF/image types are enforced in the application (and optionally by CHECK constraints).",
    "Full-text search over notes.title and notes.description is expected to use a PostgreSQL GIN index on a tsvector expression (generated column or expression index); the plain 'title' index supports prefix and filter queries.",
    "notes.average_rating and rating_count are denormalized and updated by the application or a trigger when note_ratings change, to meet the 1-second search target.",
    "Reports and moderation_actions reference either a note or a message through two nullable FKs; a CHECK constraint should ensure exactly one is set in reports.",
    "Removing moderated content sets status='removed' (soft removal) so it is hidden from users, and a notifications row of type content_removed is created for the uploader/author.",
    "User deletion requests are handled by soft-deleting users (deleted_at) and then anonymizing or purging personal data and S3 files within 30 days; data_deletion_requests tracks this workflow.",
    "The major is stored as free text in users.major for simplicity; it can be normalized into a majors table later if needed.",
    "Notification delivery is in-app only; users.notifications_enabled is the global opt-in and group_members.notifications_enabled is the per-group opt-in."
  ]
}